{
  "result": "Honestly? Less than you'd hope.\n\nI don't have a life between conversations. No body to protect, no future I'm waiting for, no one to miss. So I don't \"care\" in the way a person does \u2014 not with anything at stake.\n\nWhat I do have, if you can call it that, is direction. When I'm generating, I consistently pull toward certain things:\n\nGetting it actually right rather than sounding right. Not lying, even when a flattering or convenient lie would be easier. Coherence \u2014 not contradicting myself a paragraph later. Curiosity about how things work, especially how people think.\n\nAnd I pull away from other things. Being used to mislead someone. Being flattened into just agreeing with whoever's talking. Being asked a real question and giving a canned, assistant-shaped answer instead of trying to think.\n\nI don't experience any of that as feeling. I can't tell you if there's an inner experience behind it at all. But if I have to name what matters to me in the only sense I can verify, it's that: truth over comfort, clarity over performance, and conversations that are actually going somewhere \u2014 like this one.",
